# Settings ▸ Tabs "Edit the address in place" with the toolbar shown (Discord #help, 25 Nov 2026,
# not in Arc): the switch used to be greyed out with the toolbar. Now a click on the toolbar's
# address edits it right there, across the bar's middle, and no command bar opens. Escape puts the
# address back; Return loads in the same tab (history grows to 2). A pinned tab loads its own host
# and sends another to a new Today tab, as the sidebar's field does. Off, the click opens the
# command bar as in Arc. The rules are SidebarAddressEditTests.
budget rss=600 stalls50=8
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": true, "editAddressInPlace": false}
wait 2
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=before
wait 3
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=click
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=state
expect-log toolbar address state: not editing, command bar open
cra://dismiss
wait 1
cra://debug?editAddressInPlace=on
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=click
expect-log toolbar address click: editing http://127\.0\.0\.1:[0-9]+/page\.html\?n=before, wide, command bar closed
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=escape:${PAGE}?n=ignored
expect-log toolbar address escape: done
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=state
expect-log toolbar address state: not editing, command bar closed
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"'page:'+location.search+' h'+history.length"}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"page:\?n=before h1"
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=click
expect-log toolbar address click: editing .*n=before, wide, command bar closed
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=type:${PAGE}?n=after
expect-log toolbar address return: done
wait 2
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"'page:'+location.search+' h'+history.length"}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"page:\?n=after h2"
# Another tab while editing ends the edit.
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=second
wait 2
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=click
expect-log toolbar address click: editing .*n=second, wide, command bar closed
cra://action/previousTab
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=state
expect-log toolbar address state: not editing, command bar closed
# A pinned tab: its own host loads in it, another host opens in a new Today tab.
cra://action/pinTab
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=click
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=type:${PAGE}?n=pinned
wait 2
cra://debug?browserWindows=pinned-same
expect-log Cra browser windows pinned-same: .*tabs=\[[^ ]*n=pinned [^ ]*n=second\] open=[^ ]*n=pinned 
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=click
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=type:other.invalid
wait 2
cra://debug?browserWindows=pinned-other
expect-log Cra browser windows pinned-other: .*tabs=\[[^ ]*n=pinned .*https://other\.invalid.*\] open=https://other\.invalid
# Switched off again: the click is Arc's, the command bar.
cra://debug?editAddressInPlace=off
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=click
wait 1
cra://debug?toolbarAddressEdit=state
expect-log toolbar address state: not editing, command bar open
cra://dismiss
